= Conditional probability — Simple =

'''Conditional probability''' means the probability of something when you already know something else.

It is written:

<pre>
P(A | B)
</pre>

which means “the probability of A given B”.

For example, the chance that a card is a king changes if you already know the card is a face card.

The direction matters.

The probability of A given B is usually not the same as the probability of B given A.

Conditional probability also does not automatically tell you what causes what.

